course: dictionary
lesson: 12714
title: Dormancy: resting, not dead
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dormancy is a noun. It means a time when something is alive but not active or growing. Look at the clues around the word. «The seeds lay in dormancy all winter, waiting for spring.» Waiting for spring tells you the seeds are still alive, but they are not growing yet.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The bear went into dormancy for the cold months.» A bear that sleeps through winter is resting, not dead, so "resting through the cold months" fits. Dormancy is a resting time, not an ending.
explain: Dormancy can also describe things that are not alive. «The volcano has been in dormancy for many years.» A volcano in dormancy is quiet, but it could erupt again. So here dormancy means quiet for now, with a chance of waking up.
fact: Dormancy is a noun: a time when something is alive but resting, not active or growing.
fact: «Dormant» is the describing word, as in «The tree is dormant in winter.»
fact: Seeds stay in dormancy until they have water and warmth, and then they sprout.
fact: Some animals hibernate, which is a kind of dormancy through the cold months.
fact: A volcano in dormancy has not erupted for a long time, but it may erupt again. You can say seeds «break dormancy» when they start to grow.
exercise: «The seeds stayed in dormancy until the spring rain came.» What does dormancy mean here? | A time when the seeds were thrown away | A cold, wet puddle | *A resting time when a living thing is alive but not growing yet | A sudden burst of fast growth
exercise: «The old volcano has been in dormancy for many years, but scientists say it could erupt again.» What does this tell you? | It has never erupted before | *It is quiet now but could become active again | It is growing bigger every day | It has been destroyed for good
exercise: «The tree is dormant in winter.» Find and copy the describing word that comes from dormancy. | tree | *dormant | winter | is
test: «Bears may hibernate, which is a form of dormancy through the winter.» What is dormancy most like here? | Running fast across the hills | Eating all day long | Being completely dead | *Resting while still alive
test: «After the rain, the seeds broke dormancy and began to grow.» What does break dormancy mean? | *Stop resting and start growing | Lose all their water | Break into small pieces | Fall off the plant
exam: Which sentence shows dormancy? | *The seeds waited quietly all winter for the spring warmth | The river flowed fast after the storm | The children ran home from school | The cat jumped onto the garden fence
